Lota's Mesh patch: one statement of LÖVE's src/modules/graphics/Mesh.cpp.
Mesh's constructors allocate its vertex data with new uint8[] (lines 53 and
92), and its destructor frees it with delete (line 140), which C++ leaves
undefined for memory new[] allocated. On Linux, AddressSanitizer stops
rake test:native at the first Mesh destroyed, as an alloc-dealloc-mismatch
(doc/contributors/upstream/005.md). Nothing outside Mesh.cpp can reach that
statement: the pointer is private, and the destructor runs wherever a
Mesh's last reference goes. This patch frees it with delete[], as it was
allocated, and changes nothing else. CMake applies it to a copy of the file
at configure time (ext/lota/engine/CMakeLists.txt); vendor/love is never
written to.

diff -ruN a/src/modules/graphics/Mesh.cpp b/src/modules/graphics/Mesh.cpp
--- a/src/modules/graphics/Mesh.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/graphics/Mesh.cpp
@@ -137,7 +137,7 @@
 
 Mesh::~Mesh()
 {
-	delete vertexData;
+	delete[] vertexData;
 	if (indexData != nullptr)
 		free(indexData);
 }
